    "result_text": "Green \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, and the audit still shows the correct `NSW-16E6609E` shape.\n\n## What I changed\n\n**Finding 1 (format split from its parser) \u2014 agreed, fixed.**\n`CustomerCode` now owns both directions of the format as a matched pair:\n- Added `CustomerCode.format(region, hash8)` next to `region(...)`.\n- Introduced a single `private static final char SEPARATOR = '-'` used by both `format` (assembly) and `region` (parsing), so the dash is defined exactly once.\n- `AssignCustomerCode.service` now reads `owner.setCustomerCode(CustomerCode.format(region, hash8))` \u2014 the producer no longer hard-codes the separator independently.\n\n**Finding 2 (duplicated `\"UNKNOWN\"` sentinel) \u2014 agreed on the problem, resolved in the opposite direction from the suggestion.**\nThe suggested fix (reference `Regions.UNKNOWN` from `CustomerCode`) would have created a **package cycle**: `mapper` already depends on `model` (e.g. `OwnerMapper` \u2192 `CustomerCode`), so making `model.CustomerCode` \u2192 `mapper.Regions` would be circular. Instead I moved the canonical sentinel *down* into the model layer:\n- `CustomerCode.UNKNOWN_REGION = \"UNKNOWN\"` is now the single definition; `region(...)` returns it.\n- `Regions.UNKNOWN` now references `CustomerCode.UNKNOWN_REGION` (dependency direction `mapper` \u2192 `model`, which is already how the layers flow \u2014 no cycle).\n\nThere's now one literal, one separator, and `CustomerCode` genuinely is the single source of truth for the code's shape, its parser, and the region sentinel.",
