    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe change is well-targeted and most of it lands in the right place: `hash8`/`region` as derivations on `CustomerCode`, the audit record and membership number/check digit all flow unchanged from the single `customerCode` field, and reusing `Regions` for postcode\u2192region derivation is natural. Two structural issues, though:\n\n**1. The `<REGION>-<HASH8>` format is split from its own parser, despite the new \"single source of truth\" claim (primary).**\nThis diff upgrades `CustomerCode`'s class doc to \"Single source of truth for an owner's `customerCode` and the values derived from it,\" and adds `CustomerCode.region(code)` whose whole job is to parse the format back out by splitting on the dash. But the forward assembly \u2014 the dash separator and the `region + \"-\" + hash8` ordering \u2014 lives in `AssignCustomerCode.service` (rest.function.owner), a different class in a different package. So `CustomerCode` owns the *inverse* of the format but not the *format itself*. The `'-'` separator is now encoded independently in two classes that must agree; changing the shape means editing both, and nothing but coincidence keeps `region()`'s parse aligned with the producer.\n\nFix: give `CustomerCode` the forward factory too, e.g. `CustomerCode.format(String region, String hash8)` (or `format(Owner)`), placed next to `region(...)` so the format and its parser live as a matched pair. `AssignCustomerCode` then becomes `owner.setCustomerCode(CustomerCode.format(Regions.regionForPostcode(owner.getPostcode()), CustomerCode.hash8(...)))`, matching the class's stated role.\n\n**2. Duplicated `\"UNKNOWN\"` sentinel (secondary).**\n`Regions.UNKNOWN` is the canonical constant and `regionForPostcode` returns it, but `CustomerCode.region(code)` returns a hardcoded `\"UNKNOWN\"` literal (lines 53/49 doc) for null/no-dash codes. These are two independent definitions of the same sentinel that are only correct while they happen to match. Since `region()` is meant to read back exactly what the producer wrote, the fallback should reference the single `Regions.UNKNOWN` constant rather than re-spelling the literal.",
